From 3e18bfca43a06f31e4b23d786f71fb26b6d9e3ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:50:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Contact shadows where things meet: the new look's ambient
 occlusion

A wall's foot, the ground under eaves and carts, between roots and in a
doorway now sit in a soft shade about a yard wide, as WoW Forever's do.
Screen-space, from the depth buffer the look pass already samples
(Bevy's SSAO needs prepasses our shaders don't write): twelve taps at
half resolution with normals rebuilt from depth, a depth-aware blur,
and a depth-aware upsample in the look pass that darkens only the lit
part under 1.12's fog, weighted by how much of a pixel is ambient light.
Weaker at noon, stronger at golden hour and night, cool by day.

worldAO 0 turns it off alone; worldLook 0 is untouched 1.12.
lookao <scale 0-4> [radius] | grade holds it for film.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016HDbPQHUmJRztjWftG8oKt
